Upstream-Name: tango-devices
Comment: The package beamline-tango-devices also ships, under /opt/beamline-tango,
 the third-party Python distributions pinned in requirements/runtime.txt, installed
 unmodified from their PyPI wheels. Each one's own license text is installed with it,
 in /opt/beamline-tango/lib/python3.12/site-packages/<name>-<version>.dist-info/.
 Their licenses, as their metadata declares them: PyTango 10.3.1 (LGPL-3.0-or-later;
 bundles cppTango, omniORB, ZeroMQ), Sardana 3.7.0 and Taurus 5.4.1 (LGPL-3.0-or-later),
 numpy 2.5.4 (BSD-3-Clause and the licenses of its bundled libraries), lxml 6.1.3,
 click 8.1.6, flexparser 0.4, Pint 0.26.2, psutil 7.2.2 and pymodbus 3.15.0
 (BSD-3-Clause), flexcache 0.3 and pyserial 3.5 (BSD), docstring_parser 0.18.0,
 platformdirs 4.13.5 and setuptools 68.1.2 (MIT), packaging 24.0 (Apache-2.0 or
 BSD-2-Clause), prometheus_client 0.26.0 (Apache-2.0 and BSD-2-Clause),
 typing_extensions 4.10.0 (PSF-2.0).

